{
  "id": "permutations-ii-count",
  "questionId": "permutations-ii-count",
  "slug": "permutations-ii-count",
  "title": "Count of Unique Permutations",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Backtracking",
  "patterns": [
    "backtracking"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "instead of tracking which array positions are used, track how many of each distinct value are still available to place",
    "build a count map of value -> how many copies remain; at each position in the permutation, try placing each value that still has remaining count > 0",
    "decrement the count when you place a value and recurse to fill the next position; increment it back (undo) after that recursive branch returns",
    "count a complete permutation once every position is filled (remaining length reaches 0) - since each distinct value is only tried once per position, you never generate the same ordering twice"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using a 'used[index]' boolean array like plain Permutations, which still produces duplicate orderings when values repeat",
    "forgetting to restore (increment) the count after backtracking out of a branch, which corrupts later counts",
    "trying to sort-and-skip-adjacent-duplicates the way Subsets II does, which is trickier to get right for permutations and easy to mess up compared to the frequency-map approach"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of integers that may contain duplicate values.\n\n**Count how many distinct orderings (permutations) of the list exist.**\n\nTwo orderings that look identical (same value at every position) only count once, even if they come from swapping equal-valued elements.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "nums may contain duplicate values",
      "1 <= length of nums <= 9"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "all elements identical (answer is always 1)",
      "no duplicates at all (answer is length!)",
      "exactly one pair of duplicates among otherwise distinct values"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
